meta {
  name: Publish textbook
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/library/{{libraryItemId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "published",
    "description": "The prescribed textbook for the year. Chapters 1 to 14."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq published
  res.body.index_status: eq none
}

docs {
  Publishing is what makes an item visible to its audience, and it is the point
  where the item would be handed to the retrieval engine. It is not, here:
  RETRIEVAL_INDEX_ENABLED is off, so the item is catalogued and never
  submitted. index_status stays none, which is why folder 11 resolves this
  book to not_indexed. Turn the flag on and the same publish marks it pending
  and queues the asset for extraction.

  The audience anchors are re-checked on every write, not only on create. A
  patch that moves an item to an audience the caller cannot publish to is 403,
  and a patch that changes audience without supplying the new anchor is 400 --
  the old anchor is dropped rather than carried across, so an item cannot end
  up claiming to be section-wide while pointing at a grade.
}
